@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+# eAP-Geo v2 and EAP-LHR-JEPA-TTC protocol
+
+This branch separates two hypotheses that must not be conflated.
+
+## G2: richer transferable representation
+
+`pretrain_eap_geo_v2.py` keeps a 21-channel full-frame EventTubelet encoder for
+A0/A1 transfer and adds a 128x128 object ROI path. Auxiliary targets include
+2-D center velocity, radiality, visibility/truncation, track age, visible-area
+change, collision-corridor overlap/entry and category. Sampling is balanced by
+track-derived strata instead of choosing the nearest object at every timestamp.
+
+Because labels influence sampling, checkpoints use the distinct audited regime
+`eap_geo_v2` and declare `uses_labels_for_window_sampling=true`.
+
+### Pilot
+
+```powershell
+.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe .\scripts\pretrain_eap_geo_v2.py `
+  --root E:\eAP_dataset `
+  --inventory .\data\manifests\eap_train40_inventory_v1.json `
+  --split .\data\splits\eap_pilot12_v1.json `
+  --output .\artifacts\runs\eap_geo_v2_pilot_seed42_v1 `
+  --epochs 3 --batch-size 24 --workers 10
+```
+
+Transfer the validation-selected full-frame encoder:
+
+```powershell
+.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe .\scripts\run_evttc_architecture_matrix.py `
+  --mode screen --stage-role core --split-protocol grouped_cv `
+  --fold 0 --seed 7 --workers 10 `
+  --output-dir .\artifacts\runs\evttc32_eap_geo_v2_analysis_v1\core\fold-0 `
+  --base-initialization external_eap_geo_v2 `
+  --base-encoder-checkpoint .\artifacts\runs\eap_geo_v2_pilot_seed42_v1\eap_geo_v2_encoder_best.pt `
+  --external-pretraining-split .\data\splits\eap_pilot12_v1.json `
+  --variants A0_MATCHED_GLOBAL A1_MATCHED_DENSE_BLOCK
+```
+
+Run both folds and aggregate with the existing repository scripts. Promotion
+requires improvement in MAE, relative error and selection score versus a newly
+matched random control under the same source tree and cache manifest.
+
+## L1: deployable full-head TTC estimator
+
+`pretrain_eap_lhr_jepa_ttc.py` uses the same 40-plane, two-interval, 128x128
+object representation already materialized for EvTTC Garl arms. It predicts
+positive visible heights, applies the height-ratio equation, retains the full
+model in the checkpoint, and uses direct signed-log TTC only as secondary
+supervision. A low-weight latent predictor uses an EMA target ROI tower, while the bbox
+foreground proxy remains a training-only head.
+
+Garl labels are loaded through the repository's audited five-key join. The Geo encoder may initialize the shared EventTubelet encoder. The learned
+20-to-21 channel adapter is trained on object ROIs; no incompatible ResNet
+weight transfer is claimed.
+
+```powershell
+.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe .\scripts\pretrain_eap_lhr_jepa_ttc.py `
+  --eap-root E:\eAP_dataset `
+  --garlttc-root E:\GarlTTC_dataset `
+  --inventory .\data\manifests\eap_train40_inventory_v1.json `
+  --split .\data\splits\eap_pilot12_v1.json `
+  --geo-checkpoint .\artifacts\runs\eap_geo_v2_pilot_seed42_v1\eap_geo_v2_encoder_best.pt `
+  --output .\artifacts\runs\eap_lhr_jepa_ttc_pilot_seed42_v1 `
+  --epochs 3 --batch-size 24 --workers 10
+```
+
+Evaluate the unchanged full model zero-shot on an EvTTC cache containing
+`garl_event_roi`, `garl_delta_t_s` and `ttc_s`:
+
+```powershell
+.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe .\scripts\evaluate_eap_lhr_zero_shot.py `
+  --checkpoint .\artifacts\runs\eap_lhr_jepa_ttc_pilot_seed42_v1\eap_lhr_jepa_ttc_best.pt `
+  --cache-manifest .\artifacts\features\evttc32_paper_v6_grouped_cv_screen_core_fold0\manifest.json `
+  --splits validation `
+  --output .\artifacts\metrics\eap_lhr_zero_shot_fold0.json
+```
+
+Evaluate every held-out fold and aggregate only disjoint OOF rows before applying
+promotion gates:
+
+```powershell
+.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe .\scripts\aggregate_eap_lhr_zero_shot.py `
+  --inputs `
+    .\artifacts\metrics\eap_lhr_zero_shot_fold0.json `
+    .\artifacts\metrics\eap_lhr_zero_shot_fold1.json `
+  --output .\artifacts\metrics\eap_lhr_zero_shot_oof_analysis_v1.json
+```
+
+## Claims deliberately excluded
+
+* Public eAP 3-D reconstruction is not claimed to equal private official TTC.
+* The foreground target is a bbox proxy, not fine segmentation.
+* No RGB branch is added by this patch.
+* No SOTA claim is allowed until the protocol is frozen and benchmark-10 is
+  opened only for the final selected model.
